Types: deb
URIs: http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/
Suites: resolute resolute-updates resolute-security
Components: main restricted universe multiverse
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/ubuntu-archive-keyring.gpg

# PuralvOS is built on the standard Ubuntu archive and deliberately enables
# multiverse and restricted.
#
# Unlike dyneV, which is main-only and carries no blobs at all, PuralvOS takes
# the opposite position: use everything that works. That means proprietary
# firmware, restricted graphics drivers and unfree codecs are in scope on
# purpose. They are what makes an NVIDIA card, a Broadcom WiFi chip and a
# H.264 stream just work, and on a media workstation those are not niceties.
#
# The cost is that the image cannot claim to be free software. tools/manifest.py
# exists to keep track of exactly what non-free it carries, so the choice stays
# a decision rather than an accident.
